umiproc patch 0010: LocalMapping creates a new map point in its keyframe's map, not the atlas's current map

What: LocalMapping::CreateNewMapPoints creates each triangulated point with mpCurrentKeyFrame->GetMap() (was
mpAtlas->GetCurrentMap()). Atlas::AddMapPoint adds a point to its own map (pMP->GetMap()), so it lands there too.
Why: when tracking of an IMU-initialised map is lost, Tracking starts a new map (CreateMapInAtlas ->
Atlas::CreateNewMap) while LocalMapping may still have keyframes of the old map queued (in RECENTLY_LOST, with
IMU.InsertKFsWhenLost, Tracking inserts keyframes without waiting for LocalMapping). Each of them was triangulated
into the NEW map: points whose observations are all keyframes of the old map. At the new map's first IMU
initialisation, LocalMapping::InitializeIMU -> Optimizer::FullInertialBA(new map) adds every point of the map and,
for each observation, the keyframe's vertex. An old-map keyframe has an id below the new map's maxKFid (so it is not
skipped) but no vertex: optimizer.vertex() returns NULL and `if(!VP->fixed())` dereferences it (Optimizer.cc
FullInertialBA, mono observation). The other optimizers survive such points (BundleAdjustment skips a NULL vertex,
the local BAs keep only points of the keyframe's map), so the run went on until the new map's IMU initialisation,
which prints nothing. Upstream ORB-SLAM3 v1.0 has the same line.
Evidence: map run of episode 000128 (exit -11): right after "Creation of new map with id: 1" the new map had no
keyframe but 25 map points ("line 1873 keyframes 0MapPoints25"; only this line creates points in a map without
keyframes); the log ends at the new map's "New Map created with 145 points". On the regenerated input, a gdb
breakpoint on MapPoint::MapPoint(pos, pRefKF, pMap) with pMap != pRefKF's map caught 61 such points, all created
by the LocalMapping thread right after map 1 was created.
Behaviour change: only for keyframes LocalMapping processes after Tracking started another map: their new points
stay in the old map, with their keyframes (where its local BA, which keeps only points of the keyframe's map, now
also uses them). Nothing changes while the atlas has one map.

diff --git a/src/LocalMapping.cc b/src/LocalMapping.cc
index 4ec5e4f..fd48367 100644
--- a/src/LocalMapping.cc
+++ b/src/LocalMapping.cc
@@ -634,7 +634,10 @@ void LocalMapping::CreateNewMapPoints()
                 continue;
 
             // Triangulation is succesfull
-            MapPoint* pMP = new MapPoint(x3D, mpCurrentKeyFrame, mpAtlas->GetCurrentMap());
+            // umiproc patch 0010: the point belongs to the map of the keyframes that observe it. The atlas's current
+            // map is a different, new one when Tracking started a map while this keyframe was still queued; the point
+            // then sat in the new map with observations only in the old one (FullInertialBA segfaulted on it).
+            MapPoint* pMP = new MapPoint(x3D, mpCurrentKeyFrame, mpCurrentKeyFrame->GetMap());
             if (bPointStereo)
                 countStereo++;
             
